      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "May 11, 2026 Council action: about $8 million to Rise City Apartments (94 units, 1304 Middlefield Road, 20% to 70% AMI, 24 PSH units including 19 for adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities, construction early 2027) and a commitment to direct about $5.8 million of expected Elco Yards impact fees to MidPen Housing's 79-unit project at 1580 Maple Street (20% to 40% AMI, 23 special needs units, City-owned land transferred by the County, construction late 2027). Staff had recommended about $12.9 million for the two projects; only two applications were received. The City also runs an Affordable Housing Preservation Program (over-the-counter fund for acquisition and deed restriction; amendments adopted May 11, 2026) and is studying 70 to 104 affordable units on Downtown Library Parking Lot B (1016 Middlefield Road).",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not published; 2026 awards were about $73,000 to $85,000 per unit.",
